 ## Native qualification gate
 
-The connected card's SSH identity differs from saved trust. Native correctness, actual worker affinity and small trained-model throughput remain pending verification through a trusted console or recovery connection. No trust records or installed runtime are changed to bypass this gate. There are no new KNC tokens/sec results for this rebase, and previous-base measurements do not qualify it.
+Guarded native testing resumed on a 7120P on 2026-10-13 using the installed PhiChat 1.5.7 SSH trust and workload guard. The isolated image-fix runner has SHA-256 `e3366b50052818a7cc223f57b7b69f55316e5cd93e3ca9b67b413a849b235d54`. The installed binary and its runtime selection remain unchanged.
 
-After identity verification, run the operator and graph checks before short, alternating baseline/control/staging model runs. Use the same model hash, prompt, context, batch, worker layout and matching OpenMP library; capture full-vocabulary logits, state reset, prompt/decode timings, worker affinities and thermal guard evidence. Record source and binary hashes. Repeat on each of 3120A, 5110P and 7120P before claiming per-card native qualification.
+The image corruption came from MPSS GCC 5 emitting an inlined float metadata store through an uninitialized address register. The store wrote the projector epsilon into caller memory. A KNC-only `noinline` on the metadata getter fixes the destination without changing compute kernels. The new projector metadata regression fails before the fix and passes after it over three load/free cycles. Long absolute image-logit output paths now work.
 
-The supported compiler target is the core library, simple example and focused tests. Common/server and multimodal frontends, reasoning templates and long-context quality remain outside this qualification. Human review and maintenance ownership are required before an upstream submission, especially for the broad GCC 5 compatibility prerequisite.
+| Native check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Integrated dispatch and packed-boundary checks | 110,796 pass |
+| Graph/oracle tests, staging rows 1/2/4/8 | Pass |
+| Tiny Llama/LFM2/LFM2MoE/Qwen3, Q3/Q4/Q5_K_M; Step3 image graph; input rejections | 44 functional cases pass |
+| Staging enabled vs disabled, same KNC dot kernels | 108/108 logit files bitwise equal |
+| Installed runtime vs candidate, supported tiny Llama/LFM2 fixtures | 24/24 logit files bitwise equal; installed runner rejects the other two architectures |
+| TinyDolphin 1.1B Q5_K_M, installed runtime vs candidate | 512,032 logits bitwise equal; generated text equal |
+| Existing x86-host numerical gate | 66/108 files pass; full qualification remains blocked |
+
+The x86 comparison still uses NRMSE <= 0.002 and absolute error <= 0.03 + 0.005 * abs(reference). No tolerance was relaxed. The installed runtime reproduces the Llama Q3 and LFM2 Q4 failures. Tensor traces show small floating-point differences crossing FP16/Q8 rounding boundaries; this is separate from activation staging, which is bitwise equal to its matching KNC control. These observations do not qualify every remaining cross-host difference as harmless. Broad float-rounding experiments were rejected: they did not clear the gate and regressed trained-model throughput and logits against the installed runtime.
+
+For TinyDolphin, three alternating warmed trials used a four-token prompt, 16 output tokens, context 512, batch 16 and 180 pinned workers. Median decode throughput was 3.895 tokens/s for the candidate and 3.813 for the installed runtime; median prompt throughput was 6.374 and 6.140 tokens/s respectively. The roughly 2% decode difference is too small and the runs too short to establish a general speedup. Final-run temperatures were 52-60 C. Model worker affinity was checked at 60 or 180 threads with the whole OS core excluded.
+
+This candidate is not approved for installation: cross-host numerical qualification remains open. Native 3120A/5110P validation, trained image understanding, full-size model memory limits, reasoning templates and long-context quality are also pending. Synthetic image fixtures demonstrate graph execution and image-dependent logits, not semantic vision quality. Human review and maintenance ownership are required before an upstream submission, especially for the broad GCC 5 compatibility prerequisite.
